 ### [Grid Gradient Normal Estimation](14609-grid-gradient-normal-estimation.md)
-Computes vertex normals for a mesh (e.g., from Marching Cubes) by estimating the gradient of the underlying scalar field (density or height function) at grid vertices using finite differences, then interpolating these normals to mesh vertices. It differs from face-normal averaging by sampling the density function directly, which is considered faster or more accurate for smooth shading if the field is differentiable.
